From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emil Popovic <mail@emilpopovic.me>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Default the read-enable of read-only registers

The generated always_comb defaults every output it emits except the read
enable of read-only registers: the defaults loop skips those ports
entirely, but the port list still declares a _re_o for them. The only
read-only register is the interrupt pending array, so ip_re_o ends up
assigned in exactly one branch of the read case and held otherwise,
which infers a latch and shows up as a combinational loop in synthesis.

plic_top leaves ip_re_o unconnected, so this has no functional effect,
but the latch blocks scan insertion and trips synthesis checks.
---
 rtl/gen_plic_addrmap.py | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rtl/gen_plic_addrmap.py b/rtl/gen_plic_addrmap.py
index 2a79dc6..bcd20e6 100755
--- a/rtl/gen_plic_addrmap.py
+++ b/rtl/gen_plic_addrmap.py
@@ -84,10 +84,12 @@ class AddrMap:
     output += "  resp_o.rdata = '0;\n"
     output += "  resp_o.error = '0;\n"
     for i in self.ports:
+      # Read-only registers have no _o/_we_o, but every port has a _re_o and it needs a
+      # default like the rest, or the always_comb infers a latch on it.
       if i[3] != Access.RO:
         output += "  {}_o = '0;\n".format(i[0])
         output += "  {}_we_o = '0;\n".format(i[0])
-        output += "  {}_re_o = '0;\n".format(i[0])
+      output += "  {}_re_o = '0;\n".format(i[0])
     output += "  if (req_i.valid) begin\n"
     output += "    if (req_i.write) begin\n"
     output += "      unique case(req_i.addr)\n"
